---
description: Guidelines for creating effective Cursor rule files
glob: ".cursor/rules/**/*.mdc"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Modular: Separate files per language/domain, not monolithic
- Scoped: Use glob patterns (`*` for global, specific patterns for targeted). Globs can be comma-separated string or YAML array
- Auto-attach: Leverage globs so rules apply only where relevant
- Brutally concise: Patterns, standards, conventions, not verbose examples, only h2 for sections if required, no h1 title, avoid vague advice
- Reference internal files: Use `@` syntax to pull in existing repo docs/rules instead of re-explaining
